<title>FRANCE: France sells 22.44 bln Ffr BTANs at auction.</title>
<headline>France sells 22.44 bln Ffr BTANs at auction.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury sold the following government notes (BTANs) at auction on Thursday.</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 12.APR.99	4.75	  9.697 BLN	  3.63</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 30.887 BLN/3.2		   37 MLN	   101.85</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 30.0						    07.JUL</p>
<p> * PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL     NEXT AUCTION</p>
<p>							    N/A</p>
<p> MATURITY	COUPON	SALE AMOUNT     AVERAGE YIELD</p>
<p> 12.MAR.02	4.75	 12.746 BLN	  4.61</p>
<p> BID AMT/COVER    NON-COMPETITIVE BIDS   LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE</p>
<p> 32.346 BLN/2.5		  376 MLN	   100.57</p>
<p> PCT ALLOTED AT LOWEST PRICE*		  PAYMENT DATE</p>
<p> 80.0						    15.JUL</p>
<p> * PRICES ABOVE GOT ALLOTMENTS IN FULL     NEXT OFFER</p>
<p>							    N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - The Treasury originally announced it would sell 21 to 23 billion francs of BTANs in total. The total bid cover ratio of the auction was 2.8.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
